1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:08,000
This is School Plan Note, a web application
for elementary school teachers in Japan.

2
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:13,994
Teachers use it to write their weekly lesson
plans, manage classroom tasks, and share class

3
00:00:13,994 --> 00:00:16,000
newsletters.

4
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:25,000
This is our privacy policy — the same URL
submitted in this verification request.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:39,000
And these are our terms of service.

6
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Each teacher owns a single Google Spreadsheet
that stores their own lesson plan data.

7
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:55,173
The application is a standalone web app. It
reads and writes only this one spreadsheet,

8
00:00:55,173 --> 00:00:58,000
which the teacher selects.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:12,000
Opening the web application starts the OAuth
flow.

10
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:27,000
The application asks the teacher for
permission to access their Google data.

11
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:50,000
The teacher signs in with the Google account
they want to use.

12
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
This is the OAuth consent screen for our
application.

13
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:05,000
The address bar shows the client ID of the
OAuth client submitted for verification.

14
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:09,500
The application requests access to Google
Sheets, Drive files it creates, Classroom

15
00:02:09,500 --> 00:02:14,000
courses and announcements, sending email as
the user, and the user's email address.

16
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Each of these scopes is demonstrated in the
following sections of this video.

17
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:34,000
After the teacher grants consent, the
application opens.

18
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Teachers enter their weekly lesson plan in
this grid.

19
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:55,249
We use the spreadsheets scope only to read and
write this single database file, which is

20
00:02:55,249 --> 00:03:02,000
owned by the teacher. We never access any
other spreadsheet.

21
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Here is the same entry, written into the
teacher's own spreadsheet.

22
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:27,971
The app calls the Gemini API to draft the
class newsletter from the teacher's lesson

23
00:03:27,971 --> 00:03:30,000
plan.

24
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,746
This external HTTPS request requires the
script.external_request scope. The API key is

25
00:03:36,746 --> 00:03:42,000
stored per user in Apps Script properties and
is never shared.

26
00:03:56,000 --> 00:04:08,000
The newsletter has been generated from this
week's lesson plan.

27
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:23,247
The teacher saves the newsletter. The app
stores it in the teacher's Drive as a file it

28
00:04:23,247 --> 00:04:26,000
creates itself.

29
00:04:28,000 --> 00:04:37,463
We request the drive.file scope, not full
Drive access. The app can only see and manage

30
00:04:37,463 --> 00:04:46,000
the files it creates — it cannot read any of
the teacher's other Drive files.

31
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:57,622
Teachers can enable a daily reminder for their
unfinished tasks. Setting the delivery time

32
00:04:57,622 --> 00:05:04,000
creates a time-based trigger, which requires
the script.scriptapp scope.

33
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:17,658
The script.send_mail scope is used to send
this reminder, and userinfo.email is used to

34
00:05:17,658 --> 00:05:22,000
identify the signed-in teacher.

35
00:05:22,000 --> 00:05:35,000
As you can see, the email is delivered to the
account that is signed in. We never email

36
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:38,000
anyone else.

37
00:05:44,000 --> 00:05:50,106
We use classroom.courses.readonly only to list
the active courses the teacher already

38
00:05:50,106 --> 00:05:56,212
teaches, so they can choose one. We do not
read student data, rosters, coursework, or

39
00:05:56,212 --> 00:05:58,000
grades.

40
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,362
When the teacher clicks this button, the app
posts the schedule to the selected course as

41
00:06:06,362 --> 00:06:12,000
an announcement. This is what the
classroom.announcements scope is used for.

42
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:23,392
Here is the announcement in Google Classroom.
The teacher always initiates the post — the

43
00:06:23,392 --> 00:06:30,000
app never posts without an explicit action by
the teacher.

44
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:37,385
All requested scopes are used only for these
purposes, as described in our privacy policy.

45
00:06:37,385 --> 00:06:41,000
Thank you for reviewing our application.
